{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>I am the El of Beit El.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): who revealed Himself to you at Beit El." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: this angel who called himself El is the Good, as it is said (Exodus 33:19): ״אני אעביר כל טובי על פניך״ — and He is the House concerning which it is said of Him (Numbers 12:7): ״בכל ביתי נאמן הוא״, for the good — the man is his house. And therefore he said of himself: 'I am the El of Beit El.' And likewise concerning Jacob: ״ויקרא למקום אל בית אל״. And behold, this verse is sound according to its plain sense, for this angel who is El is Beit El. And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:37.401211449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}